  "continuity": "All 127 domain cases passed before the initial data compilation stopped on a new fixture parameter-name warning under -Werror. Production source is unchanged between gates. Only two test files differ: matching the overridden roomId parameter and excluding device-specific unsigned acknowledgements from fresh/old event equality while asserting actual ciphertext events. All 27 selected data/provider/native cases and quality checks pass on 8451 unchanged final inputs.",
  "evidence": [
    "Existing room policy still validates exact canonical own Matrix member, account, space, server and creator. Fresh devices now require only their own HRISG_ namespace, allowing an admitted original canonical user. Retained HRIS_ devices keep exact legacy tuple validation.",
    "Four group cursor tests include fresh devices in SPACE/LEGACY rooms, bidirectional old-company/old-group cursor replay rejection and mismatched user/account/device/legacy metadata.",
    "Actual Synapse tests retain original room events after restart and register fresh devices on new and original users. Original sender/ciphertext/device IDs remain, event/context reads succeed, cursor replay fails, and old-device access still works. Existing company/group projection regressions pass.",
    "Actual native registration, activation, bootstrap and admitted history event run for both fresh canonical-user kinds, with exact provider credential and outside-SQL I/O plus zero request leases. Its room/provider values are explicit fixtures; eight unchanged native history tests separately exercise real PostgreSQL room access and revocation."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No fresh-device SDK Megolm recovery/decryption is claimed. Original event identity excludes device-specific unsigned transaction acknowledgement differences.",
    "No schema, application DI graph or HTTP parser changes. Group rollout remains disabled and all 54 PRD acceptance groups remain open.",
    "Combined original/group read scope, old queued key identity lookup, sync/metadata/push, Mobile SDK adoption and native hard-parent recovery remain required.",
    "Live8b40/schema116 push on/SMTP off, normal phone28, Mobile product/hosted0b804cb2 and Starter9959c1d unchanged."
